    <string name="disclaimer_title">Before you start</string>
    <string name="disclaimer_body">EasyLink and EasyBridge devices are experimental amateur LoRa radio communication equipment.\n\n1. COMMUNICATION IS NOT GUARANTEED. LoRa is a best-effort radio channel: messages, calls and SOS may fail due to terrain, interference, low battery or distance. The device is NOT a satellite beacon and does NOT replace rescue services, cellular networks or professional communications.\n\n2. DO NOT rely on it as your only means in a life-threatening situation. Always have a backup plan and share your route.\n\n3. RADIO REGULATIONS. Transmit power and allowed frequencies differ by country. You are responsible for keeping the device settings compliant with your local laws. High power and some frequencies require a licence.\n\n4. The developers and Yvak Inc. are not liable for any damage, injury, loss of communication or your violation of radio regulations.\n\nBy tapping “Accept” you confirm you have read and agree.</string>
    <string name="disclaimer_accept">Accept</string>
    <string name="disclaimer_decline">Exit</string>
    <string name="disclaimer_link">Full terms: yvak.inc</string>

    <string name="set_expert">Expert mode</string>
    <string name="expert_enable">Enable expert mode</string>
    <string name="expert_hint">Unlocks high transmit power and modes that may be illegal in your country. All responsibility is yours.</string>
    <string name="expert_warn_title">Expert mode</string>
    <string name="expert_warn_body">High power (27–30 dBm ≈ 0.5–1 W) and some frequencies require a licence and are banned in most countries without permission. Operating outside the law is your responsibility. Enable?</string>
    <string name="expert_on">On — full power available</string>
    <string name="expert_off">Off — safe power only</string>
    <string name="tx_power_locked">High power — expert mode only</string>
    <string name="tx_power_legal_hint">Low power is safer and usually legal. Higher — per your country\'s law.</string>
    <string name="sos_disclaimer">SOS is best-effort and may not arrive. Not a replacement for rescue services.</string>

    <string name="antenna_warn_title">⚠️ ANTENNA FIRST</string>
    <string name="antenna_warn_body">Do NOT power the device on without a tightly screwed antenna. Transmitting without an antenna, or with a loose one, can permanently burn the RF stage.</string>
    <string name="antenna_warn_short">Before powering the device: make sure the antenna is screwed on tight!</string>

    <string name="ob_next">Next</string>
    <string name="ob_done">Let\'s go!</string>
    <string name="ob1_t">1. Antenna → power</string>
    <string name="ob1_b">Screw the antenna on tight, and only then power the EasyBridge on. Transmitting without an antenna can burn the radio.</string>
    <string name="ob2_t">2. Connect</string>
    <string name="ob2_b">Profile tab → Connect → pick your EasyBridge from the list. The link stays alive even with the app minimized.</string>
    <string name="ob3_t">3. Talk</string>
    <string name="ob3_b">Write to the General channel — everyone in range hears it. Voice notes, photos, radio calls, SOS — all without cellular. Answers live in Settings → Help.</string>

